MODULE PB-OPS-CONVENTIONS — Raw MAC/s, T-ops/s, Effective Ops, Precision & Checks
==========================================================================================================

=====================================================================================
THROUGHPUT CONVENTIONS (MAC vs FLOPs) + RESULTS (derived from time)
=====================================================================================
- MAC definition: one multiply–accumulate. We report RAW T-MAC/s (hardware rate).
- T-ops/s = 2 × T-MAC/s if you count multiply and add separately.
- Algorithmic multiplier: k = 1 (no algorithmic scaling). Set env ALG_K to add effective ops columns.

Precision & Scaling:
- Arithmetic: INT8 × INT8 → INT32 accumulate; dyadic shift = 2^-(fracA+fracB) with fracA=4, fracB=4 ⇒ 2^-8.
- Overflow guardrail (clamp ±120): |∑ a_k b_k| ≤ K·(120^2) must be < 2^31. Shapes:
  • 5120×5120×5120   K=5120    bound≤73,728,000    int32_safe=True
  • 128×128×128      K=128     bound≤1,843,200     int32_safe=True
  • 192×192×192      K=192     bound≤2,764,800     int32_safe=True
  • 256×256×256      K=256     bound≤3,686,400     int32_safe=True

